-------------------------------------------------------

  https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold
  release v1.1.4, commit eab85828
  Copyright 2026 TensorFold contributors

  Apache License, Version 2.0:                  LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt
  MIT notice for code written before 0.6.0:    LICENSES/TensorFold-MIT.txt
  TensorFold's NOTICE, kept as Apache-2.0 s4(d) requires:
                                               LICENSES/TensorFold-NOTICE.txt
  TensorFold's third-party notices:            LICENSES/TensorFold-THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md

  Statement of changes, Apache-2.0 s4(b). The patches below modify TensorFold's
  source and quote it as diff context. They were made by edison in October 2026,
  are not part of any TensorFold release, and are not endorsed by TensorFold:

    patches/0002-windows-arm64-port.patch
      5 files: zig/kernels/cuda/qmm_prefill.cu, prefill_attention.cu,
      gdn_prefill.cu, zig/src/families/flashnext/cuda_ple_reader.zig and
      cuda_ple.zig. MSVC compatibility only. In the three .cu files the sole
      change is adding __restrict__ to the argument lists of explicit template
      instantiations, so they match the definitions the host compiler sees; not
      one kernel body, launch dimension or arithmetic expression is touched. The
      two .zig files change only how Zig 0.17's platform declarations are read
      (std.posix.MAP and CLOCK are void there).

    patches/0003-load-pipeline.patch
      4 files. Host-side loader only: zig/src/families/flashnext/cuda_modelopt_experts.zig,
      cuda_prompt_wt.zig, cuda_prompt.zig and zig/src/core/nvfp4_slice.zig.
      Staged parallel expert packing, pinned double buffering, a wider shard
      mapping cache, whole-row copies. Touches no .cu file and no kernel launch
      configuration.

  The modified TensorFold code stays under TensorFold's licenses (Apache-2.0, and
  the MIT notice for code written before 0.6.0). This repository distributes the
  diffs only -- never a modified TensorFold tree, never a built binary. Anyone who
  applies them and builds gets a TensorFold binary and must ship TensorFold's
  LICENSE, LICENSES/, NOTICE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md with it.


4. Deliberately not redistributed here
--------------------------------------

  Model weights. The default checkpoint, nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP4-Local, is
  NVIDIA's quantization-aware-distilled FP4 export of Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next and
  is used under the NVIDIA Open Model Agreement
  (https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/agreements/enterprise-software/nvidia-open-model-agreement/);
  the base model is under the Qwen Community License 1.0
  (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/blob/main/LICENSE). You accept
  those terms when you download the weights; this repository only names the repo
  and revision to fetch.

  Compiled artifacts. tensorfold-native.exe, tf-cuda-test.exe, *.cubin, *.pdb and
  build/ are all in .gitignore. A binary built with these patches is a TensorFold
  binary under TensorFold's licenses (section 3), not under this repository's MIT.

  libtfgrammar.so, xgrammar and dlpack. Structured output is served by TensorFold's
  own release archive; nothing of it is fetched, modified or redistributed by this
  repository. Its notices travel with TensorFold (LICENSES/TensorFold-THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).

  The Zig compiler. scripts/5-build.ps1 downloads Zig 0.17.0 at build time and
  invokes it; the toolchain is not redistributed here. Zig is MIT (Expat),
  Copyright (c) Zig contributors, https://ziglang.org -- used at build time only.

  The recipe's container image, and the Python packages scripts/4-venv.ps1 installs
  (transformers, PyAV, Pillow and their dependencies). Nothing of it is redistributed
  here; the venv is built from public indexes on the machine that runs it.


